# SRG-APP-000374-AU-000290  -  CAT III
# Upon receipt of the log record from hosts and devices, the Central Log
# Server must be configured to record time stamps of the time of receipt
# that can be mapped to Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000374-AU-000290
group:           V-206504
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001890
control_rev5:    AU-8

contribution:    Splunk stamps _indextime on every event at the point its receiver accepts
                 it and stores event time as an epoch value, which is UTC by construction.
                 The application's configurable share is whether that receipt-time range is
                 tracked and returned to search, and how the record's own timestamp is
                 recognized and mapped to UTC.

governs:         limits.conf - Limits on how much work searches and data processing may consume.
governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.

check:           limits.conf [search] track_indextime_range in 1|true
check:           props.conf [<source type>] DATETIME_CONFIG not_equals NONE
check:           props.conf [<source type>] TIME_FORMAT non_empty
check:           props.conf [<source type>] TZ non_empty
check:           props.conf [<source type>] TZ_ALIAS present

external:        The host clock that splunkd reads, and its synchronization to an
                 authoritative time source, are provided by the operating system and the
                 time service.
external:        Whether the sending host's own timestamp is accurate rests on that host;
                 Splunk records the time it received the record, not the sender's clock
                 discipline.

citation:        limits.conf.spec:315 [search], :929 track_indextime_range = <boolean>
                 default true; props.conf.spec:502 DATETIME_CONFIG = [<filename> | CURRENT
                 | NONE], :554 TIME_FORMAT, :580 TZ, :592 TZ_ALIAS. No condition is written
                 over limits.conf durable.track_time_type: that key is not declared in the
                 staged specification set, so its vocabulary cannot be confirmed.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: DATETIME_CONFIG is set to NONE
                 for an audit source type, or TIME_FORMAT and TZ are unset so the record's
                 timestamp is not deterministically mapped to UTC, or track_indextime_range
                 is disabled so the receipt time is not returned to search.
